\ Registers an `#in?` arm for arrays, the key the prelude already fills. Running this file raises
\ duplicate-method on that arm. Checking or linting it reports the diagnostics below the arm instead
\ of aborting on it.

#in?: method{ array any } [ [ = ] curry #any ] ;

bad-decl: ( -- x ) [ 1 2 ] ;

no-effect: [ 1 ] ;
